Create one original transparent RGBA production spritesheet for Moxie Capwell's right-facing basketball fall action. Follow the supplied Moxie portrait and gameplay references as strict identity and anatomy guides: adult human woman, pale skin, lavender-purple eyes, very long thick lavender high ponytail with small gold tie, mature athletic build, purple-and-silver uniform with white side panels, purple wristbands and purple high-tops. Same face, eyes, ponytail/tie, and kit in every pose.

1990s arcade basketball pixel-cel art, crisp outlines, consistent scale. Exact 1536x1024 canvas, 5 columns x 2 rows, ten complete Moxie poses row-major in every cell. Wide clear transparent gutters; no clipped ponytail, hands or shoes. Moxie alone. No ball or opponent drawn: the separate basketball will be handled by the game. No floor, shadow, court, hoop, effects, glow, background, text or labels. Return true-transparent RGBA with alpha-zero background.

A controlled nonviolent basketball stumble-and-fall with safe athletic form, no injury or distress. Pose sequence:
0: off-balance recovery step after a loose-ball collision, arms out;
1: stumble forward, one foot catches, hands spread;
2: drop center, bend knees and reach one hand toward the floor;
3: knee touches down and opposite hand braces;
4: controlled side fall, hip lowers, ponytail arcs behind;
5: settle onto side with one palm supporting her, legs bent;
6: seated on hip, one hand plants, other hand visible and empty;
7: turn to one knee;
8: rise into a low crouch;
9: recover to balanced standing guard, calm face.
Keep complete human anatomy, all poses distinct and sequential, no impact marks or visible injury.
